AEM – Content Fragment vs Experience Fragment

Content Fragment (CF)

A Content Fragment is structured and reusable content that is independent of page presentation.

Example: Product name, description, price and specifications.

Experience Fragment (XF)

An Experience Fragment is a group of components combined to create a reusable experience.

Example: Website header, navigation menu and promotional banner.

Key Differences

Content Fragment| Experience Fragment
Structured content| Group of components
Content-focused| Experience-focused
Content Fragment Model| Experience Fragment Template
Supports headless delivery| Supports reusable page experiences

Key Takeaway

Content Fragments manage reusable content, whereas Experience Fragments manage reusable content experiences.

